(6559211, 976045, 30861, '<td valign="top">Nit-pick time; the actual Frost quote is "The woods are lovely, dark and deep..." with only one comma. The woods have two qualities; "dark and deep" is seen as a single quality in support of "lovely". With the second comma, "dark" and "deep" are separated into distinct attributes, not what Frost intended.<br/> <br/>None of this impacts my judgment of the image (it''s quite nice) and you may not care at all, but in case you do... :-)</td>', 'Nit-pick time; the actual Frost quote is "The woods are lovely, dark and deep..." with only one comma. The woods have two qualities; "dark and deep" is seen as a single quality in support of "lovely". With the second comma, "dark" and "deep" are separated into distinct attributes, not what Frost intended. None of this impacts my judgment of the image (it''s quite nice) and you may not care at all, but in case you do... :-)', '2011-10-03 11:52:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6559213, 976857, 30861, '<td valign="top">Uncle Tim''s Bridge, Wellfleet? Linda? Denise? Doesn''t look like Nicky''s style, but I guess I have to add him to the list. I know it''s not me or Penny. Or maybe it''s not really Uncle Tim''s Bridge? ''Cuz if it IS, that''s a heck of a color throw on the leaves :-)</td>', 'Uncle Tim''s Bridge, Wellfleet? Linda? Denise? Doesn''t look like Nicky''s style, but I guess I have to add him to the list. I know it''s not me or Penny. Or maybe it''s not really Uncle Tim''s Bridge? ''Cuz if it IS, that''s a heck of a color throw on the leaves :-)', '2011-10-03 11:58:00.000000', NULL, 1),
